# Beat: guided walk through bob/logfile against googleapis.desc,
# with the overrides from alice/app.desc already loaded.
#
# Invocation:
#   protolens --descriptor-set $PROTOTEXT_GOOGLEAPIS_SET bob/logfile \
#       --load-overrides alice/overrides \
#       --script beats/googleapis.desc
#
# Re-pin (must print nothing):
#   protolens --descriptor-set $PROTOTEXT_GOOGLEAPIS_SET bob/logfile \
#       --load-overrides alice/overrides \
#       --script beats/googleapis.desc script \
#     | grep 'error:'

title: The logfile, googleapis.desc

steps:
  - text: |
      This is bob/logfile reopened — this time against the full googleapis descriptor set.

      Good, our overrides have been correctly re-loaded.

      👋 Press `2` to unfold more of the logfile.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    node: /
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - visible: /3/4

  - text: |
      Now protolens shows proposals for fields 6 and 7.

      Let's hover over the heat cue for field 7.
      Protolens proposes ComputeRoutesResponse which feels reasonable.

      👋 Press `t` for the override menu and commit ComputeRoutesResponse v2.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/4
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /3/4 google.maps.routing.v2.ComputeRoutesResponse

  - text: |
      Similarly with field 6.
      ComputeRoutesRequest v2 feels right.

      👋 Press `t`for the override menu and commit ComputeRoutesRequest v2.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /3/3 google.maps.routing.v2.ComputeRoutesRequest

  - text: |
      👌 Perfect, we're done with making sense of the log file.

      Now there seems to be a couple of issues with the protobuf:
      See the amber cues?
      Let's have a closer look... 🔍

      👋 Click the amber triangle to unfold the compute_routes_request node.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - visible: /3/3/3

  - text: |
      Look at the travel_mode field:
      The amber diamond and the ohb annotation (ohb for OverHangingBytes)
      mean that the encoding for the DRIVE value uses too many bytes

      Show wire-level information for a closer look.

      👋 Press `w` to show wire-level information.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/3/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - wire: /3/3/3

  - text: |
      Indeed, the wire-level encoding uses 5 bytes for encoding the value 1.
      A normal encoding would have used a single byte (0x01).
      Weird.

      👋 Press `w` again to hide wire-level information.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/3/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3/3
    wire_line: /3/3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - not:
        - wire: /3/3/3

  - text: |
      Now let's have a second look at the shadowed SearchTextRequest field.

      Hover on the heat cue at the left edge of the line.
      protolens reckons that the string actually might be a google.rpc.Status message.

      👋 Press Enter to commit the proposed google.rpc.Status override.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_line: true
    command: override /1/3/1 --as google.rpc.Status --cardinality optional --field-name status
    advance_when:
      - type: /1/3/1 google.rpc.Status

  - text: |
      🚨 Indeed... That is very suspicious.
      The unmasked google.rpc.Status message even includes an API key 😠

      👋 Press space to step.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/3 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_node: true
    search: 'value: ".*"'

  - text: |
      Let's save our findings:
      Export the full logfile as prototext format
      for sending back to Bob.

      👋 Press Enter to commit the prefilled export command.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /
    command: export --prototext alice/logfile.all.node.pb
    advance_when:
      - file_exists: alice/logfile.all.node.pb

  - text: |
      Now press Enter to quit.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /
    command: quit
